## Oh-My-Research (omr) plugin

The omr plugin is enabled in this workspace
(https://github.com/Tianyi-Billy-Ma/Oh-My-Research). It ships
research-oriented skills and MCP servers for autoresearch / viberesearch
workflows in Claude Code.

### Skills

Invoke via `/omr:<name>`:

- `setup` — install, configure, and health-check omr. The umbrella entry
  point for any "I just enabled this plugin, now what?" question.
- `doctor` — read-only diagnostic. Verifies plugin integrity, MCP wiring,
  CLAUDE.md install state, token presence, HPC config drift, and external
  dependencies. Points at `/omr:setup` for any fix.

Run `/omr:setup --help` for the current list. New skills land here as the
plugin grows; the slash-command prefix is always `omr:`.

### MCP servers

Five servers declared in the plugin's `.mcp.json`:

- `exa`, `tavily`, `brave-search` — web search (stdio, fetched via `npx`).
- `github` — GitHub APIs (HTTP, requires `GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN`).
- `huggingface` — Hugging Face Hub (HTTP, requires `HF_TOKEN`).

Token resolution: shell env first, then project-local `.env` (stdio servers
only — HTTP servers read shell env only). Never echo or persist token
values; use `/omr:setup` to audit.

### Conventions

- Plugin namespace is `omr` (short for Oh-My-Research). The full name lives
  in the description; `omr` is the slash-command prefix everywhere.
- Project-scoped omr state (if any) lives at `.omr/` (gitignored).
- **Always use the `AskUserQuestion` tool for user-facing questions.**
  Consent prompts, scope choices, conflict resolutions, branch decisions —
  every interactive question goes through `AskUserQuestion` with explicit
  options, never a plain-text "what do you want to do?" left for free-form
  reply. This applies inside omr skills and to any other interaction in a
  session where omr is enabled.

### Where to learn more

- `/omr:setup` for first-time configuration and health checks.
- Plugin README at https://github.com/Tianyi-Billy-Ma/Oh-My-Research.
